# Five classes override the method, which is too many to tell apart by comparisons. The receiver's shape word is the index into a table of methods, and the call goes to the address found there.
# CHECK-LABEL: name="areaOf" role=Source
# CHECK-NEXT: BB#0:
# CHECK-NEXT: Int64 b@[[shape]] = ArgumentReg(
# CHECK: Int32 b@[[word]] = Load(b@[[shape]], offset = 12, ControlDependent|ReadsImmutable|Reads:AOTObject_shapeWord, {{*}}:CallTable)
# CHECK: Int32 b@[[entry]] = Load(b@{{*}}, {{*}}Reads:AOTInstance_mutableFields, {{*}}:CallTable)
# CHECK: Int64 b@[[base]] = Load(b@{{*}}, {{*}}Reads:AOTInstance_fixedFields, {{*}}:CallTable)
# CHECK: Int64 b@[[address]] = Add(b@[[base]],
# Every method of the name returns a number, and flow says at the call that a number comes back: it comes back as a double in a register, whichever entry of the table is entered.
# CHECK-NEXT: Double b@[[area]] = Patchpoint(b@[[shape]]:Register({{*}}), b@[[address]]:Register({{*}}), resultConstraints = Register({{*}}), {{*}}:CallTable)
# CHECK-NOT: Branch(
# CHECK-NOT: IToD(
# CHECK-NOT: BitwiseCast(
# CHECK: Double b@[[sum]] = Add(b@[[area]],
# CHECK-NEXT: Return(b@[[sum]], Terminal)
# CHECK-LABEL: end of function
# Nothing compares the shape word, reads a prototype or looks the name up.
# NONE-LABEL: name="areaOf" role=Source
# NONE-NOT: = Equal(
# NONE-NOT: PrototypeLinks
# NONE-NOT: :CallDirect)
# NONE-NOT: :PropGet)
# NONE-LABEL: end of function
# X64: instructions: 7, patchpoints: 1
# ARM64: instructions: 11, patchpoints: 1
